#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Run the orders-recovery workshop. Every command checks before it acts, and says what to do next.

Read-only (nothing in AWS or Clumio changes):
  ./lab preflight            is this account ready for the workshop?
  ./lab status               Clumio's recovery points, and whether the incidents can start
  ./lab check                HEALTHY or BROKEN: every order is there, unchanged, with its intact document
  ./lab portal               one order at a time, at http://localhost:8080 (Ctrl-C stops it)
  ./lab report               the scorecard (each incident's time to HEALTHY), and .lab/report.html

Changes:
  ./lab seed                 loads 1,000 orders and their documents (terraform apply runs it)
  ./lab break deploy         a bad deployment: deletes 100 orders, overwrites 50 documents (once Clumio holds copies)
  ./lab break everything     deletes the database, the bucket and every version (asks first)
  ./lab prepare NAME         makes a restored cluster queryable (instance, RDS Data API)
  ./lab repair --from NAME   copies only the missing orders back from a restored cluster
  ./lab repair --from-csv F  copies only the missing orders back from a Clumio record-restore CSV
  ./lab drop NAME            deletes a restored cluster you no longer need
  ./lab rebuild              recreates the empty documents bucket for Clumio to restore into
  ./lab down                 deletes everything the workshop made (asks first), then checks it is gone

Settings: terraform.tfvars (account_id, region), CLUMIO_API_TOKEN and CLUMIO_API_BASE_URL in your
shell. Names: names.json, shared with Terraform. Needs terraform, the AWS CLI v2 and python3.
"""

